  "statement": "Using the binomial expansion, show that for small $x$, $\\sqrt{1+x}\\approx1+\\tfrac12x-\\tfrac18x^{2}$, and use this to estimate $\\sqrt{1.02}$ to four decimal places.",
  "solution": "$(1+x)^{1/2}=1+\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac{(1/2)(-1/2)}{2}x^{2}+\\cdots=1+\\tfrac12x-\\tfrac18x^{2}+O(x^{3})$. With $x=0.02$, $\\sqrt{1.02}\\approx1+\\tfrac12(0.02)-\\tfrac18(0.02)^{2}=1+0.01-0.00005=1.00995$, i.e. $1.0100$ to four decimal places.",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
  "hints": ["Write down the binomial expansion to x^2.", "Substitute x=0.02.", "Evaluate the three terms."]
}
